From 50bf829548b6211581fd7c3f32dec7b10f1cfed2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@MyComputer.localdomain>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 17:08:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/38] Connect DFLASH to ReplaySSM fold-every-commit for GDN
 models (PR #36683, hand-ported)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DFlash commit scatters intermediate_ssm snapshots that ReplaySSM mode no
longer produces, so the guard in _build_hybrid_req_pool rejected GDN.
Route the DFlash post-verify commit through the common
commit_mamba_states_after_verify hook (fold-every-commit from the
per-slot raw-input ring) when the pool has replayssm_spec_fold set; the
legacy snapshot path stays for non-ReplaySSM runs. The guard now only
rejects DSPARK+GDN on non-static ragged layouts.

This frees the per-draft full-state snapshot scratch (~8G on 12-slot
DFlash) at the cost of an fp32/bf16 fold per commit — accuracy A/B
required before production (bf16 re-quantization drift).
